Day 1 (February 14, 2024): Arrival in Madrid and Exploring the City Center

* Arrive at Adolfo Suárez Madrid–Barajas Airport
* Take a taxi or metro to your hotel in the city center (approximately €20-€30)
* Check-in to your hotel and freshen up
* Visit the nearby Puerta del Sol, a famous square in the heart of Madrid
* Walk to the nearby Plaza Mayor, a historic square with beautiful architecture
* Enjoy traditional Spanish tapas and drinks at a local bar

Day 2 (February 15, 2024): Art and Culture

* Start the day at the Prado Museum, one of the world's greatest art museums ( tickets: €20)
* Explore the museum's extensive collection of European art, including works by Goya, Velázquez, and El Greco
* Visit the nearby Reina Sofia Museum, home to Picasso's Guernica (tickets: €15)
* Enjoy lunch at a local restaurant serving traditional Spanish cuisine
* Spend the afternoon strolling through the Retiro Park, a beautiful green space in the heart of the city

Day 3 (February 16, 2024): Royal Palace and Gardens

* Visit the Royal Palace of Madrid, an impressive palace with stunning gardens (tickets: €12)
* Take a guided tour of the palace and learn about its history
* Explore the adjacent Sabatini Gardens, a beautiful park with fountains and walking paths
* Enjoy lunch at a local restaurant serving traditional Spanish cuisine
* Spend the afternoon shopping for souvenirs or exploring the nearby Plaza de Santa Ana

Day 4 (February 17, 2024): Day Trip to Toledo

* Take a day trip to the historic city of Toledo (approximately €30-€40 by train)
* Visit the Cathedral of Toledo, a beautiful Gothic church
* Explore the narrow streets and alleys of the old town, lined with shops and restaurants
* Enjoy lunch at a local restaurant serving traditional Spanish cuisine
* Return to Madrid in the evening

Day 5 (February 18, 2024): Flamenco Show and Tapas Crawl

* Attend a flamenco show at a local tablao (approximately €20-€30)
* Experience the passion and energy of traditional Spanish music and dance
* Visit several bars for a tapas crawl, sampling local specialties like patatas bravas and tortilla española
* Enjoy dinner at a Michelin-starred restaurant serving modern Spanish cuisine

Day 6 (February 19, 2024): Day Trip to Segovia

* Take a day trip to the historic city of Segovia (approximately €30-€40 by train)
* Visit the Roman Aqueduct and the Segovia Cathedral
* Explore the narrow streets and alleys of the old town, lined with shops and restaurants
* Enjoy lunch at a local restaurant serving traditional Spanish cuisine
* Return to Madrid in the evening

Day 7 (February 20, 2024): Shopping and Relaxation

* Spend the morning shopping for souvenirs or exploring the nearby Gran Vía, a bustling shopping street
* Visit the nearby Thyssen-Bornemisza Museum, home to an impressive collection of European art (tickets: €15)
* Enjoy a relaxing afternoon at a local spa or wellness center
* Enjoy a farewell dinner at a Michelin-starred restaurant serving modern Spanish cuisine

Transportation:

* Use taxis or metro to get around the city (approximately €2-€5 per ride)
* Take trains to Toledo and Segovia for day trips (approximately €30-€40 per trip)

Dining Options:

* Try traditional Spanish tapas at local bars like El Qu Jetcho or La Terraza
* Enjoy modern Spanish cuisine at Michelin-starred restaurants like El Pichón or Mugaritz
* Sample local specialties like patatas bravas and tortilla española at food stalls or markets

Note: Prices are approximate and subject to change.


